  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "da600000-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# DAG Notebook\n\nThis notebook uses the **DAG Notebook** layout (\u0060Verso.Showcase.DagNotebook\u0060, installed automatically the first time you open it). It looks and works like the regular notebook, with one addition: cells that share variables are linked.\n\n- A chip like \u0060\u2191 2 unitPrice\u0060 means this cell reads \u0060unitPrice\u0060 from cell 2; \u0060\u2193 4 revenue\u0060 means cell 4 reads \u0060revenue\u0060 from this one. Click a chip to jump to the linked cell.\n- When a cell finishes running, the cells downstream of it re-run automatically, in dependency order.\n- A cell whose inputs ran more recently than it did shows a dashed border until it catches up.\n\nRun everything once with **Run DAG** in the header, then try the experiment further down."
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0002-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "// The base inputs. Everything below derives from these two values.\nvar unitPrice = 24.99;\nvar unitsSold = 1200;\nvar unitsOrdered = 2;\nConsole.WriteLine($\u0022{unitsSold} units at {unitPrice:C}\u0022);"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0003-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var revenue = unitPrice * unitsSold;\nConsole.WriteLine($\u0022Revenue: {revenue:C}\u0022);"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0004-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var costRatio = 0.62;\nvar profit = revenue * (1 - costRatio);\nConsole.WriteLine($\u0022Profit: {profit:C}\u0022);\nConsole.WriteLine($\u0022Ordered: {unitsOrdered}\u0022);"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0005-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var summary = $\u0022Sold {unitsSold} units for {revenue:C}, keeping {profit:C} in profit.\u0022;\nConsole.WriteLine(summary);"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0006-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Try it\n\nChange \u0060unitPrice\u0060 in cell 2 to \u006029.99\u0060 and run just that cell. Revenue, profit, and the summary re-run on their own, in order. Then toggle **Auto-run dependents: Off** in the header and repeat: this time the downstream cells only mark themselves stale (dashed border) and wait for you.\n\n## When the layout refuses to guess\n\nThe two cells below both assign \u0060counter\u0060, so there is no single producer to link. Each gets a warning chip instead of an edge, and \u0060counter\u0060 never participates in auto-run."
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0007-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "var counter = 0;"
    },
    {
      "id": "da600000-0008-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "counter = counter \u002B 1;\nConsole.WriteLine($\u0022counter is now {counter}\u0022);"
    }
  ],
  "layouts": {
    "com.verso.showcase.dag-notebook:dag-notebook": {
      "autoRun": true
    }
  }
}